<h1 class="ct-art-title">Designing a conference identity that scales across 50+ assets</h1>
<p class="ct-art-dek">NECLive 2025: one fingerprint, shaped into a continent, carried from screens into the venue.</p>
<div class="ct-art-meta"><img alt="" src="/img/team-subomi.webp"/><span>Olasubomi Archibong</span><span class="dot"></span><span>5 min read</span></div>
</div>
<img alt="NECLive 2025 conference identity: one fingerprint, scaled to 50+ assets" class="ct-art-cover" src="/img/work-neclive-v4.webp"/>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section ct-art-body">
<div class="container w-layout-blockcontainer">
<div class="ct-art-col">
<div class="ct-art-stats">
<div><b>50+</b><span>Assets in one visual language</span></div>
<div><b>1</b><span>Core idea, carried everywhere</span></div>
<div><b>3</b><span>Channels: digital, social, venue</span></div>
<div><b>300+</b><span>Attendees on the day</span></div>
</div>
<p class="ct-art-lead">NECLive's 2025 theme was Powering Africa Through Creative Enterprise. Our job was to turn that idea into a visual identity that could speak to a pan-African audience, sit inside NECLive's existing brand and hold together across dozens of sponsor-heavy assets.</p>
<h2>The challenge</h2>
<p>The central question was simple to ask and hard to answer: how do you design for Africa without flattening its complexity? Designing for a continent demands thought, restraint and respect for meaning, not aesthetics alone. Three constraints shaped the brief.</p>
<ol class="ct-art-list">
<li><b>Cultural depth, no clichés.</b> No spectacle, no power symbols, no overused Afrocentric motifs.</li>
<li><b>One anchor that scales.</b> A concept strong enough to hold every asset together.</li>
<li><b>Built for volume.</b> Flexible across digital, social and the venue, and clear in layouts crowded with sponsor logos.</li>
</ol>
<div class="ct-art-figs two"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="NECLive 2025 key art: a This Way street sign over the fingerprint pattern" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-keyart.webp"/><figcaption>Edition key art: “This way”, celebrating African creativity.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="This Way sign on a black background" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-this-way.webp"/><figcaption>The sign became a recurring wayfinding device.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>The idea: a fingerprint, shaped into a continent</h2>
<p>Creativity in Africa is lived, inherited and shared, so the metaphor had to be grounded in collective humanity. We landed on the fingerprint: universally understood as a mark of identity, authorship and human presence. Its lines flow outward into patterns and form the map of Africa, so creativity reads as a people-powered force rather than a machine.</p>
<blockquote class="ct-art-quote">Africa's creative enterprise is powered by the people who shape it. Our identity is our power.</blockquote>
<div class="ct-art-figs one"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="The African fingerprint map pattern in pink, green and black" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-fingerprint.webp"/><figcaption>The hero pattern: fingerprint lines that resolve into Africa.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>The system</h2>
<h3>1. An edition identity inside the existing brand</h3>
<p>We kept NECLive's typographic system for continuity and gave 2025 its own signature: a lockup with the fingerprint map built in, and the theme line warped into the silhouette of Africa so the words themselves carry the message. The fingerprint map also stands alone as a hero graphic.</p>
<h3>2. One pattern, many surfaces</h3>
<p>The fingerprint became the base texture for banners, announcements, reels, story templates and speaker features, in three colourways: purple, pink and lime. It gave every asset a recognisable rhythm without making them look identical.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs one"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="NECLive 2025 event banner in purple with the theme lettering" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-banner.webp"/><figcaption>Event banner: speakers, date and venue on the purple colourway.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h3>3. Templates built for volume</h3>
<p>Speaker cards, partner announcements, banners and posters all came from one modular kit. The team could keep up with frequent updates, and every layout stayed legible, even with a full sponsor strip along the bottom.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs three"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Pink theme poster: Powering Africa Through Creative Enterprise" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-poster-theme.webp"/><figcaption>Theme poster.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Host feature card for Tee A on purple" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-poster-host.webp"/><figcaption>Host feature.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Creative partner announcement on purple" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-poster-partner.webp"/><figcaption>Creative partner announcement.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>The results</h2>
<p>On 28 November 2025 the identity left the screen and wrapped the Landmark Centre in Lagos: entrance, booths, corridors and the main stage. More than 50 assets shared one visual language, the theme came through without clichés, and NECLive 2025 showed up as a confident platform for Africa's creative future in front of 300+ attendees.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs two"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="NECLive letters at the Landmark Centre entrance" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-venue-2.webp"/><figcaption>The entrance at the Landmark Centre.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Main stage panel at NECLive 2025" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-venue-1.webp"/><figcaption>Panel on the main stage.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="ct-art-figs three"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Booth wall with Africa is now lettering" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-venue-3.webp"/><figcaption>Booths.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Corridor with colour-block wall" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-venue-4.webp"/><figcaption>Corridors.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Lime fingerprint panel at the venue" loading="lazy" src="/img/nec-venue-5.webp"/><figcaption>Venue panels.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>What we took from it</h2>
<ul class="ct-art-list">
<li><b>Find the human metaphor first.</b> A symbol people already understand travels further than a clever graphic.</li>
<li><b>Design the system, not the poster.</b> One pattern and one modular kit made 50+ assets fast and consistent.</li>
<li><b>Plan for the room.</b> An identity that works on a phone and on a 10-metre wall is one that holds together.</li>
</ul>
